&lt;p&gt;Astoria, Oreg&oacute;n &ndash; La oficina del Departamento de Servicios Humanos de Oreg&oacute;n (ODHS) en Astoria, situada en 422 Gateway Avenue, cerrar&aacute; el viernes 13 de marzo de 1:00 a 5:00 por trabajos de construcci&oacute;n programados en el &aacute;rea. Sin embargo, la Camioneta de Beneficios M&oacute;vil de ODHS estar&aacute; disponible para atender a quienes necesiten servicios en persona. Tambi&eacute;n se puede acudir a la oficina de ODHS en Seaside, 1111 Roosevelt Drive.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Las personas tambi&eacute;n pueden acceder a ODHS de forma virtual, llamando:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
     &lt;li&gt;Programa de Bienestar Infantil para cuidado de crianza, seguridad infantil y servicios de adopci&oacute;n, 503-325-9179.&lt;/li&gt;
     &lt;li&gt;Programas de Autosuficiencia, Asociaci&oacute;n de Elegibilidad de Oreg&oacute;n para beneficios de comida, dinero, servicios m&eacute;dicos, cuidado infantil y servicios de violencia dom&eacute;stica. 503-325-2021.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;"Tendremos personal en estas ubicaciones alternativas para atender a las personas, ya sea en persona o virtualmente", dijo Lorena Giles, Gerente de Programa OEP.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Vancouver, Wash.&amp;nbsp;&ndash; The Neighborhood Associations Council of Clark County recently awarded two Public Works employees with the Outstanding Clark County Employee award, in recognition of their service to the community.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The Neighborhood Associations Council of Clark County is a program of the county&rsquo;s neighborhood outreach program in the county manager&rsquo;s office. The council is comprised of representatives from various active neighborhood associations in unincorporated Clark County.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Since 2005, the council has awarded a county employee with the Outstanding Clark County Employee award to recognize county employees who have demonstrated exceptional service to and collaboration with the community. The award &ldquo;&hellip;recognizes a county employee who exemplifies professionalism, expertise, service, and an unwavering commitment to the people and communities of Clark County.&rdquo; Due to scheduling conflicts, the group presented both its 2024 and 2025 awards at the Clark County Council meeting on Tuesday, March 3.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2024 recipient: Hunter Decker, county forester&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
The Neighborhood Associations Council noted Decker&rsquo;s efforts to go &ldquo;&hellip; out of his way to be friendly, approachable and helpful&hellip;&rdquo; Neighbors appreciate his commitment to public safety and support for rural communities. &ldquo;In every sense, Hunter represents the very best of public service: knowledgeable, responsive, community-minded, and deeply committed to the well-being of Clark County and its residents.&rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Upon accepting the award, Decker noted that he grew up in Clark County and was honored to serve the community. &ldquo;I didn't think I would get a little emotional, but I just always wanted to give back to this county&hellip; And I'm going to just keep continuing helping the county the best I can&hellip;&rdquo; Decker said.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2025 recipient: Eric Lambert, Clean Water Outreach Services manager&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Eric Lambert was nominated for his leadership in making a local resident&rsquo;s dream a reality. After a neighbor shared a vision of a community effort to beautify a frequently vandalized retaining wall, Lambert led a team of staff and volunteers to create the Salmon Creek Mural in just a few months. &ldquo;Neighborhood association members appreciate Eric&rsquo;s willingness to listen, act upon ideas and suggest improvements.&rdquo; The nomination highlights his collaborative spirit and ability to bring together many ideas and voices into one unified effort.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;After receiving the award, Lambert thanked the community, noting that &ldquo;One of the things I like to do most in life&hellip; [is] connecting with the community.&rdquo; He spoke about the friendships and connections formed among strangers as they volunteered for the community project, and noted, &ldquo;&hellip; that&rsquo;s a really special thing that will go to live on.&rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Residents can learn more about the county&rsquo;s forestry program on the &lt;a href="https://clark.wa.gov/public-works/sustainable-forestry-program"&gt;county&rsquo;s sustainable forestry webpage&lt;/a&gt;. An interactive webpage about the Salmon Creek Mural project, with photos, videos and artist information, is also available on the &lt;a href="https://clark.wa.gov/public-works/salmon-creek-mural"&gt;county&rsquo;s website&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For information about road and park projects, closures, opportunities for community input, and more, residents can follow Public Works on &lt;a href="https://twitter.com/ClarkCoWa_PW"&gt;X&lt;/a&gt; (formerly known as Twitter), &lt;a href="https://www.facebook.com/clarkcowa.pw/"&gt;Facebook&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="https://www.instagram.com/clarkcowa_pw/"&gt;Instagram&lt;/a&gt; and view information on Nextdoor. Residents can also visit &lt;a href="https://clark.wa.gov/public-works"&gt;clark.wa.gov/public-works&lt;/a&gt; to sign up for email notifications.&lt;/p&gt;

