&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:16px"&gt;&lt;span style="color:rgb(36, 36, 36); font-family:arial,arial_embeddedfont,arial_msfontservice,sans-serif"&gt;On Wednesday March 11, the Portland Metro Chamber and the Black Business Association of Oregon (BBAO) will host a&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a class="Hyperlink SCXW165312617 BCX0" href="https://community.portlandmetrochamber.com/chamber-events/Details/breakfast-forum-state-of-black-business-in-oregon-1635714?sourceTypeId=Website" rel="noreferrer noopener" style="-webkit-user-drag: none; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; user-select: text; text-decoration-line: none;" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;span style="color:rgb(70, 120, 134); font-family:arial,arial_embeddedfont,arial_msfontservice,sans-serif"&gt;Breakfast Forum&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style="color:rgb(36, 36, 36); font-family:arial,arial_embeddedfont,arial_msfontservice,sans-serif"&gt;&amp;nbsp;on&amp;nbsp;the current state of Black enterprise&amp;nbsp;across the state, focused on&amp;nbsp;policy and systems.&amp;nbsp;Join&amp;nbsp;to hear in-depth&amp;nbsp;assessments of&amp;nbsp;where Black-owned businesses are today,&amp;nbsp;which strategies and investments are producing measurable impact, and&amp;nbsp;the policy, procurement, and institutional changes&amp;nbsp;required&amp;nbsp;to accelerate sustainable growth and wealth creation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:rgb(36, 36, 36); font-family:arial,arial_embeddedfont,arial_msfontservice,sans-serif"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

